---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE, repoIssueUrl } from '../config';
---
<Base title="Contact & Support" description={`Contact the ${SITE.name} team for bug reports, tool requests, security disclosures, or general inquiries.`}>
  <article class="policy-card prose">
    <span class="badge badge-accent">Get in Touch</span>
    <h1>Contact {SITE.name}</h1>
    <p class="lede">Have a question, found a bug in a Kubernetes validator, want to suggest a new DevOps tool, or need to reach us regarding privacy or partnerships? Choose the fastest channel below.</p>

    <div class="contact-grid">
      <section class="contact-box">
        <h2>Direct Email</h2>
        <p>For general inquiries, privacy requests, content corrections, or sponsorship questions:</p>
        <p class="contact-action"><a class="btn" href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a></p>
        <p class="muted small">We typically respond within 2–3 business days.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="contact-box">
        <h2>GitHub Issues &amp; Contributions</h2>
        <p>For reproducible bugs, edge cases in YAML/JSON parsing, new tool requests, or prompt submissions, GitHub Issues let the community track fixes transparently:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><a href={repoIssueUrl('bug_report.yml')} rel="noopener">Report a bug</a></li>
          <li><a href={repoIssueUrl('tool_request.yml')} rel="noopener">Request a new tool</a></li>
          <li><a href={repoIssueUrl('prompt_submission.yml')} rel="noopener">Submit an AI prompt template</a></li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </div>

    <h2>Security disclosures</h2>
    <p>If you discover a security vulnerability—such as a Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) issue, a Content Security Policy bypass, or a secret-redaction flaw—please review our <a href={`${SITE.repo}/blob/${SITE.branch}/SECURITY.md`} rel="noopener">Security Policy</a> or email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a> with <code>[SECURITY]</code> in the subject line before opening a public issue.</p>

    <h2>Before reporting a tool bug</h2>
    <p>Never include real production passwords, bearer tokens, or private keys in a bug report or email. Replace sensitive values with synthetic placeholders (or run them through our <a href="/tools/k8s-redactor/">Kubernetes Redactor</a> first) and include your browser version and expected vs. actual output.</p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .policy-card {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius-l);
    padding: 2rem 2.25rem;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
    max-width: 54rem;
  }
  .policy-card h1 {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: 1.06rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
  .contact-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem;
  }
  .contact-box {
    background: var(--bg-subtle);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius-m);
    padding: 1.25rem 1.35rem;
  }
  .contact-box h2 {
    margin-top: 0;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
  }
  .contact-action {
    margin: 1rem 0 0.75rem;
  }
  .small {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .contact-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .policy-card {
      padding: 1.35rem;
    }
  }
</style>
